      "message": "The OTA will generate artifacts. So doing fstrim earlier will just discard blocks that will then be used. That \"duplicate\" work seemed unnecessary.\n\nThe original design for A/B is to be applied during idle maintenance. The update modules (inside GMS) doesn\u0027t always honor that, so there are anyways bugs open because dex2oat might be felt. I don\u0027t think the 30s (compared to 20-25m average OTA time) are significant.\n\nAs GMS doesn\u0027t honor idle-maintenance, that might not happen before reboot.",
